{"id": "11498", "key": "CAFBSS-880", "self": "https://cafb-hungerbangers.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/11498", "expand": "operations,versionedRepresentations,editmeta,changelog,renderedFields", "fields": {"votes": {"self": "https://cafb-hungerbangers.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/CAFBSS-880/votes", "votes": 0, "hasVoted": false}, "labels": [], "status": {"id": "10102", "name": "Closed", "self": "https://cafb-hungerbangers.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/status/10102", "iconUrl": "https://cafb-hungerbangers.atlassian.net/", "description": "(Migrated on 5 Apr 2025 15:04 UTC)", "statusCategory": {"id": 3, "key": "done", "name": "Done", "self": "https://cafb-hungerbangers.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/statuscategory/3", "colorName": "green"}}, "comment": {"self": "https://cafb-hungerbangers.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/11498/comment", "total": 1, "startAt": 0, "comments": [{"id": "11469", "body": "10/01/2024 10:13;61536ea272f6970069fc1dbd;Good morning Mitilde,

I hope you are doing well. Thank you for sharing your feedback with us; it is very valuable. I will follow up with the Transportation Leadership Team to address the way the drivers communicate with partners about this issue.

To provide some context, there are two main reasons why drivers may not take pallets when dropping off food during a delivery. Firstly, they may have food for an immediate order or need to pick up food from another site for the warehouse, which means they cannot have food and pallets on the truck at the same time due to food safety (Pallets are often leftoutside- on the ground, possibly in the rain, and are often dirty) and consideration for our partners. Secondly, our drivers may be on tight schedules and do not have the time for a pallet pickup due to their busy delivery schedules, especially during the busy season.

There is no reason why a driver could not explain this to you at the time, and I will ensure that this information is communicated to them. I apologize for your experience. 

Thank you,

"D"
10/01/2024 10:21;61536ea272f6970069fc1dbd;I spoke with the Transportation Supervisor, and she mentioned that she received feedback about the pallets not being stacked properly and having trash around them. She has scheduled a pallet pickup for tomorrow. Please make sure that the pallets are stacked together to allow the equipment to pick them up easily, there is no debris around them, and they are placed on concrete, not on grass. Thank you!
10/01/2024 10:43;qm:65d20c5a-0c84-458e-8ce1-adb90d07460f:0263e065-5e9f-426c-8230-43d43b0d7e07;!image3.jpeg|thumbnail!

This is how the pallets were placed. We canâ€™t stack them any higher, so we have to put them to the side due to our limited space. The driver was rude, which is unusual, as weâ€™ve always had great relationships with all the other drivers.
Thanks for picking the pallets soon. 
Matilde  


