{"id": "11786", "key": "CAFBSS-865", "self": "https://cafb-hungerbangers.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/11786", "expand": "operations,versionedRepresentations,editmeta,changelog,renderedFields", "fields": {"votes": {"self": "https://cafb-hungerbangers.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/CAFBSS-865/votes", "votes": 0, "hasVoted": false}, "labels": [], "status": {"id": "10102", "name": "Closed", "self": "https://cafb-hungerbangers.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/status/10102", "iconUrl": "https://cafb-hungerbangers.atlassian.net/", "description": "(Migrated on 5 Apr 2025 15:04 UTC)", "statusCategory": {"id": 3, "key": "done", "name": "Done", "self": "https://cafb-hungerbangers.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/statuscategory/3", "colorName": "green"}}, "comment": {"self": "https://cafb-hungerbangers.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/11786/comment", "total": 1, "startAt": 0, "comments": [{"id": "11987", "body": "09/13/2024 10:30;712020:b15fa988-bc60-49b4-aa6f-e30b7a3629c1;Good morning,

Thank you for contacting customer support. I reached out to our Technical Support team to look into why the chicken was not able to be added to orders. Please note that by the time you tried to add the item to your order it was already sold out, showing 0 available for the date you selected. We apologize for any confusion as it is a feature of our website to update/remove sold out items off the website at midnight the day they sell out. 

